WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.636
Safe query APIs are one of the main reasons developers use ORMs.

2
00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:14.131
Filtering by values, creating records, updating fields, deleting records,
joining relationships, and paginating results can often be expressed
without hand-built SQL strings.

3
00:00:14.131 --> 00:00:18.521
The ORM or database driver can bind values separately from query
structure.

4
00:00:18.521 --> 00:00:24.695
That separation is what prevents ordinary data values from being
interpreted as database command syntax.

5
00:00:24.695 --> 00:00:28.194
Parameter binding remains important even when using an ORM.

6
00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:37.386
When developers stay within normal value-based filter methods and prepared
statement concepts, the data layer can pass values safely to the database
driver.

7
00:00:37.386 --> 00:00:47.264
When developers build raw fragments, concatenate conditions, or insert
user-controlled strings into query methods that expect structure, they may
leave the safe path.

8
00:00:47.264 --> 00:00:52.752
Safe ORM use depends on knowing which API accepts values and which API
accepts query structure.

9
00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:57.142
SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE operations all need safe construction.

10
00:00:57.142 --> 00:01:07.638
Bulk operations deserve special care because they can affect many records
and may bypass model hooks, validation paths, or per-object checks
depending on the ORM and usage pattern.

11
00:01:07.638 --> 00:01:09.833
Query composition also needs review.

12
00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:19.779
A helper that adds filters, joins, or conditions should preserve parameter
binding and authorization assumptions, not quietly replace them with
unsafe string assembly.

13
00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:28.766
The safest standard is simple: use structured ORM APIs for values, use
parameters for raw SQL values, and avoid mixing untrusted data into query
structure.

14
00:01:28.766 --> 00:01:38.438
If a feature genuinely needs dynamic structure, such as selecting a sort
column or report field, that decision belongs in an allowlisted mapping,
not in raw user input.

15
00:01:38.438 --> 00:01:43.240
Safe query construction should be the default behavior in every data-
access path.
